.el .ds Aq '
.TH quarters-rollback 1  "quarters-rollback " 
.SH NAME
quarters\-rollback \- Replace a Quarter from a snapshot after capturing recovery
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBquarters\-rollback\fR [\fB\-\-preview\fR] [\fB\-\-confirm\-space\fR] [\fB\-\-confirm\-replace\-state\fR] [\fB\-\-exclude\-recovery\-cache\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fB\-\-recovery\-name\fR> <\fITARGET\fR> <\fISNAPSHOT\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Replace a Quarter from a snapshot after capturing recovery
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-\-recovery\-name\fR \fI<NAME>\fR
Name for the automatic pre\-rollback recovery snapshot
.TP
\fB\-\-preview\fR
Validate all sources and bounds without creating or replacing state
.TP
\fB\-\-confirm\-space\fR \fI<SPACE>\fR
Exactly repeat SPACE to confirm the target
.TP
\fB\-\-confirm\-replace\-state\fR \fI<SPACE>\fR
Exactly repeat SPACE to acknowledge complete home replacement
.TP
\fB\-\-exclude\-recovery\-cache\fR
Omit derived caches from the automatic recovery snapshot
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fITARGET\fR>
Target Quarter whose identity will be retained
.TP
<\fISNAPSHOT\fR>
Snapshot display name to restore
